# sweep-liquid-gpu.steps -- liquids and the translucent world through the
# SDL_GPU backend (-gpu) against GL (#340 P3a): opaque and translucent water,
# the vanilla liquid-alpha contract, lava with and without r_lavaalpha, the
# per-pixel UV warp, and a camera under the water looking up at its surface.
# All of it draws through GL_ImmEnd (EmitWaterPolys) and P2's seams; what
# P3a changes is the three GL-only paths beside it, gated off under -gpu (see
# tools/test_rg_sources.py).
#
# Run the SAME binary both ways, with identical settings:
#
#   A="-fsaa 0 +gamma 1 +map demo1"
#   STEPS=tools/sweep-liquid-gpu.steps ENGINE=$E ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/l-gl  ~/hexen2 $A
#   VK_ICD_FILENAMES=<lvp_icd json> STEPS=tools/sweep-liquid-gpu.steps ENGINE=$E \
#       ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/l-gpu ~/hexen2 -gpu +gpu_allow_software 1 $A
#
# then the three checks (the 200x24+100+576 mask is the mini status bar's
# health, as in tools/sweep-world-gpu.steps):
#
#   1. GL against -gpu, every frame:
#        PSNR_MIN=42 ./tools/shot-diff.sh /tmp/l-gl /tmp/l-gpu 200x24+100+576
#   2. The vanilla contract, on EACH side: only *lowlight and *rtex078 are
#      translucent; *rtex346, demo1's gold pool, is opaque whatever
#      r_wateralpha says (R_LiquidAlpha, gl_rsurf.c).  Cameras 01 (0.33) and
#      02 (1) hold both pools, so the gold pool must be pixel-identical
#      between them and the *rtex078 pool behind the doorway must not:
#        magick compare -metric AE -crop 160x60+290+205 /tmp/l-gpu/01-pools.png \
#            /tmp/l-gpu/02-pools-wa1.png null:     # gold pool: 0
#        magick compare -metric AE -crop 586x200+214+368 /tmp/l-gpu/01-pools.png \
#            /tmp/l-gpu/02-pools-wa1.png null:     # *rtex078: thousands
#   3. Nothing unrouted: between each REPORT-<map>-BEGIN and -END in
#      /tmp/l-gpu/qconsole.log, gpu_unrouted counts 0 calls into the GL
#      entry points.
#
# With the Vulkan validation layers on (VK_LAYER_PATH=<vulkan-validation-layers>
# /share/vulkan/explicit_layer.d, +gpu_debug 1) the -gpu run must log no
# "Validation Error".
#
# SETTINGS.  On top of tools/sweep-world-gpu.steps' list (what -gpu does not
# draw yet, and what makes a frame repeatable), on BOTH sides:
#   r_oit 0              OIT is P6; -gpu takes sorted blending whatever it says
#   r_waterwarp 0        the underwater screen warp is a post-process pass (P4)
#   r_softparticles 0    the soft-particle depth snapshot is P4
#   r_softemu 0, r_scale 1   post-process (P4)
#   gl_waterwarp_speed 0 the turbulence follows realtime, which a pause does
#                        not stop; 0 freezes the warp at its t=0 phase
#   r_caustics 0         the underwater caustics follow realtime too (they
#                        only draw with the camera in water)
#   gl_glows 0           glows are P3b
#   r_drawviewmodel 0    the view model hides the pools
#   r_drawentities 0     entities move or spin while the game runs, so a
#                        pause catches them at a run-dependent pose: a weapon
#                        spins in the gold pool, village3's mana and knight
#                        (35 dB GL against -gpu with them drawn, every
#                        differing pixel on them).  On demo1 it
#                        also takes away the func_door between the two pools.
# Every camera is a noclip setpos (no fall, no water current) with the game
# paused for the shot.  A map change leaves the console down (the toggle
# typed after "map" is lost in the load), hence the bare "console" after
# each one.
#
# CAMERAS.  Placed with a BSP29 leaf check and ray march of the world hull
# (camera eye in an EMPTY leaf, or WATER for 07-09, 12 units clear all round;
# the liquid's faces in the frustum and in sight), then checked by eye:
#   01-03  demo1, the *rtex078 pool in front and the *rtex346 gold pool
#          beyond the doorway, one view: r_wateralpha 0.33, 1, and 0.33 with
#          r_water_pixel_warp 1.  (From the gold pool's side the glyphs
#          around it fill the frame, and they are an animated texture whose
#          frame a pause catches at random: 38 dB GL against -gpu, every
#          differing pixel on them.)
#   04-06  demo1, the *lowlight pool (its bridge is an entity, so not
#          drawn): the same three
#   07-09  demo1, under that *lowlight water, looking up at the surface:
#          r_wateralpha 0.33 and 1 with the contents tint off, then 0.33
#          with it on (R_PolyBlend).  The setpos origin is z -520 and the
#          leaf is CONTENTS_WATER from z -600 up past -440 (the surface is
#          z -432), so the eye is under water at any view height up to 80;
#          09's tint is the engine's own confirmation, it is drawn only for
#          a liquid view leaf (V_SetContentsColor)
#   10-12  castle4, the *lava000 pit: r_lavaalpha 0 (opaque), 0.5, and 0.5
#          with r_water_pixel_warp 1
#   13-14  village3, the *lava000 trough: r_lavaalpha 0 and 0.5
#   15-16  village3, the *lowlight trough: r_wateralpha 0.33 and 1
#
# THE THRESHOLD.  From three runs a side, as shot-diff.sh's header asks.
# Measured 2026-11-20, 800x600, llvmpipe GL against lavapipe -gpu (Mesa
# 26.2), PSNR in dB, masked:
#
#   camera              GL vs -gpu, runs 1/2/3   GL vs GL      -gpu vs -gpu
#   01-pools            51.56 51.50 67.02        47.56 50.32   50.84 51.43
#   02-pools-wa1        48.90 48.66 67.05        45.97 47.68   50.84 48.63
#   03-pools-pixelwarp  51.55 51.48 67.00        47.57 50.34   50.84 51.41
#   04..06 lowlight     51.42 .. 76.97           50.11 .. 52.16  51.44 .. identical
#   07..09 under        51.95 .. 78.17           50.72 .. 53.98  51.97 .. identical
#   10..12 castle4      49.27 .. 67.68           49.00 .. 50.17  49.14 .. 50.11
#   13..16 village3     49.20 .. 53.66           49.36 .. 52.09  49.21 .. 53.88
#
# (GL vs GL is no tighter than GL vs -gpu: the pools camera still sees a few
# of the animated glyphs, and a pause catches every animated texture at a
# run-dependent frame; the runs where both sides caught the same frames read
# 63-78.)  What the gate exists to catch, by proxy -- the -gpu frame of the
# neighbouring setting against the GL frame, i.e. -gpu dropping that setting:
# r_wateralpha 1 drawn as 0.33 19.3 (pools), 21.0 (lowlight), 21.4 (from
# below), 31.1 (village3); r_lavaalpha 0.5 drawn opaque 19.0 / 20.6;
# r_water_pixel_warp ignored 23.1 (lava), 33.7 (pools), 37.1 (lowlight);
# the contents tint dropped 19.0.  So 42 dB: 4 dB under the worst honest
# pair (45.97, GL against GL), 5 dB over the best broken one (37.1).  The
# gate is for the Mesa pair; a hardware pair needs its own three runs.


sleep 20
cmd god
cmd notarget
cmd noclip
cmd viewsize 120
cmd crosshair 0
cmd showpause 0
cmd r_skyspeed_back 0
cmd r_skyspeed_front 0
cmd r_flatlightstyles 1
cmd r_dynamic 0
cmd r_gpulightstyles 0
cmd r_ssao 0
cmd r_bloom 0
cmd r_dlight_occlusion 0
cmd r_alias_gpu 0
cmd r_particles 0
cmd fog 0
cmd gl_texture_anisotropy 1
cmd r_oit 0
cmd r_waterwarp 0
cmd r_softparticles 0
cmd r_softemu 0
cmd r_scale 1
cmd gl_waterwarp_speed 0
cmd r_caustics 0
cmd gl_glows 0
cmd r_drawviewmodel 0
cmd r_drawentities 0
cmd r_wateralpha 0.33
cmd r_lavaalpha 0
cmd r_water_pixel_warp 0
sleep 2

# --- demo1: both pools, the vanilla contract ---
cmd setpos -1007 2200 -442 25 152 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 01-pools
cmd r_wateralpha 1
shot 02-pools-wa1
cmd r_wateralpha 0.33
cmd r_water_pixel_warp 1
shot 03-pools-pixelwarp
cmd r_water_pixel_warp 0
cmd pause

# --- demo1: *lowlight under the bridge ---
cmd setpos -1800 1700 -330 45 200 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 04-lowlight
cmd r_wateralpha 1
shot 05-lowlight-wa1
cmd r_wateralpha 0.33
cmd r_water_pixel_warp 1
shot 06-lowlight-pixelwarp
cmd r_water_pixel_warp 0
cmd pause

# --- demo1: under the *lowlight water, looking up ---
cmd gl_cshiftpercent_contents 0
cmd setpos -2000 1600 -520 -50 90 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 07-under
cmd r_wateralpha 1
shot 08-under-wa1
cmd r_wateralpha 0.33
cmd gl_cshiftpercent_contents 100
shot 09-under-tint
cmd pause

# --- demo1 report, on the pools camera ---
cmd setpos -1007 2200 -442 25 152 0
sleep 2
cmd gpu_unrouted reset
sleep 2
cmd echo REPORT-DEMO1-BEGIN
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd renderer_status
cmd echo REPORT-DEMO1-END
sleep 1

# --- castle4: the lava pit ---
console
enter map castle4
sleep 20
cmd god
cmd notarget
cmd noclip
cmd setpos 1652 1496 -646 20 88 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 10-c4-lava
cmd r_lavaalpha 0.5
shot 11-c4-lava-la05
cmd r_water_pixel_warp 1
shot 12-c4-lava-la05-pixelwarp
cmd r_water_pixel_warp 0
cmd r_lavaalpha 0
cmd pause
cmd gpu_unrouted reset
sleep 2
cmd echo REPORT-CASTLE4-BEGIN
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd renderer_status
cmd echo REPORT-CASTLE4-END
sleep 1

# --- village3: the lava and *lowlight troughs ---
console
enter map village3
sleep 20
cmd god
cmd notarget
cmd noclip
cmd setpos 1442 220 372 30 310 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 13-v3-lava
cmd r_lavaalpha 0.5
shot 14-v3-lava-la05
cmd r_lavaalpha 0
cmd pause
cmd setpos 1074 388 357 25 272 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 15-v3-lowlight
cmd r_wateralpha 1
shot 16-v3-lowlight-wa1
cmd r_wateralpha 0.33
cmd pause
cmd gpu_unrouted reset
sleep 2
cmd echo REPORT-VILLAGE3-BEGIN
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd renderer_status
cmd echo REPORT-VILLAGE3-END
sleep 1
